{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/agents/formats/README.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:53:46.646421Z","id":"5676a59310cc6d6a73f4c269b9355894290edbe78ce6119f75350ee5be0606c9","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath-goldens/tests/observed.rs fails when a recording adds a field, an entry type or a version the notes don't name. A change to a reader or writer that alters what toolpath reads or writes, without a new recording, is not caught: the ir/document/projection snapshots change, but nothing ties that diff to the note. Whole-file qualifier spans on each provider.rs/project.rs would enforce it (any edit drifts until re-anchored after checking the note) but would fail every concurrent piece that touches those files; not done. A cheaper link: have the observed test also diff the ir@<set> key paths against a per-harness 'fields toolpath reads' table in observed/.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":102},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"380177978b1023ebafe4ade58c0bd12db6abc3cae65c2a57e375e848e2734c83"},"summary":"The Maintenance rule is enforced from the recordings, not from the code","tags":["format-notes","gap","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
